# ComposePlatform — Glossary [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

> The load-bearing terms, defined once and pointed at their owning specs. Read a term here to orient;
> follow the pointer for the full contract. Terse by design — a term that needs a paragraph earns its
> own spec node, and this entry points at it.

---

## Substrate & Bus

### [GLOSS-BUS] ComposeBus / the Bus

- term: ComposeBus (colloquially "the bus")
- definition: the typed publish/subscribe fabric every peer communicates over. Namespace-addressed (address by message, not by node — CAN-Bus DNA); no peer holds a reference to another. Scope is `local` (in-process) or `global` (bridged over a transport, MQTT at `mqtt-broker.local:1883`). Messages are `state` (current value, retained — a late subscriber still sees current state) or `command` (imperative, drives undo).
- lives-in: `layers/composeio` (`io` domain)
- see-also: [GLOSS-STATE-ENGINE], [GLOSS-NARROW-WAIST]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-STATE-ENGINE] State Engine

- term: state engine
- definition: the typed state machine a namespace carries — not a raw variable but a type + range + valid transitions (`binary`, `tri_level`, `stop_light`, `continuous_0_255`, `enum`, `json`). A value that violates the engine is a HARD ERROR, not a coercion. Free-form strings (paths, IDs, selections) MUST use the `json` engine — a strict engine fed an out-of-domain value (classically `""` into `binary`) raises inside a Tk callback and can abort the process.
- lives-in: `layers/composeio` (`io` domain)
- see-also: [GLOSS-BUS]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-BUS-STORAGE] bus:// and doc://

- term: bus-native storage (`bus://`, `doc://`)
- definition: the platform's storage seams, addressed like bus namespaces. `bus://assets/<path>` resolves bytes via bus_storage (`:8420`); `doc://<collection>/<id>` resolves/queries documents via document_store (`:8421`). The client resolver is `composeio.resolve` (`resolve_bytes`, `resolve_doc`, `put_doc`, `query_docs`). Images/assets load by reference (`bus://`), never inlined.
- lives-in: `layers/composeio` (`io` domain), `families/services` (`svc` — the store daemons)
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

---

## Render & Contract

### [GLOSS-CANVAS-CONTRACT] Canvas Contract

- term: Canvas contract
- definition: the EXPLICIT narrow-waist rendering contract — ~30 named primitives every backend meets. A widget definition renders pixel-identically across backends (macOS, RPi, browser, CYD) because every format lowers TO this contract and every backend is EXTENDED to meet it. Contrast the bus contract, which is (today) implicit — a named wart ([INSIGHT-BUS-CONTRACT-IS-IMPLICIT]).
- lives-in: `layers/composeux` (`ux` domain)
- see-also: [GLOSS-NARROW-WAIST], [GLOSS-COMPOSE-YAML]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-NARROW-WAIST] Narrow Waist

- term: narrow waist
- definition: the single shared contract everything meets at, so N formats × M backends collapses to N + M. Formats lower TO the waist; backends are extended to MEET it; a widget is reused BY REFERENCE, never forked to a backend. The Canvas contract is the render-layer narrow waist; a declared, typed, versioned bus contract would be the same discipline one layer over.
- lives-in: `platform` (`plt`) — the pattern; `layers/composeux` — the Canvas instance
- see-also: [GLOSS-CANVAS-CONTRACT]
- relates-to: [DX-NARROW-WAIST]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-COMPOSE-YAML] .compose.yaml

- term: `.compose.yaml`
- definition: the declarative authoring format for a ComposeUX surface/widget — the config-over-code artifact a builder emits instead of writing Python. It lowers to the Canvas contract; the SDR credo made concrete (specificity in configuration, not firmware).
- lives-in: `layers/composeux` (`ux` domain)
- see-also: [GLOSS-CANVAS-CONTRACT]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

---

## Identity & Intelligence

### [GLOSS-INTELLIGENCE-PEER] Intelligence-as-Peer

- term: Intelligence-as-peer
- definition: the credo that an Intelligence drives every surface IDENTICALLY to a human — every builder/operator action is a bus message, a mouse drag and an MCP publish are peers, and no privileged back door exists. If a capability is not reachable over the bus, the design is incomplete. Inherited by every surface built with Composer.
- lives-in: `layers/composeio` (`io`), `families/apps/intelligence-console` (`app.console`)
- see-also: [GLOSS-SELF-ID]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-SELF-ID] self/<id>/*

- term: `self/<id>/*` (carried identity)
- definition: the proposed completion of the decomposition to the observer. The Intelligence's own state (`context`, `memory`, `projects`) is today a SINGLETON namespace (`self/*`) that a console must GUESS the owner of; `self/<id>/*` with an identity PASSED (not guessed) makes the Intelligence a true peer in the namespaces. An open wart, not yet built.
- lives-in: `families/apps/intelligence-console` (`app.console`); the thesis in `platform`
- relates-to: [INSIGHT-SELF-IS-NOT-YET-A-PEER], [PLT-INTELLIGENCE-PEER]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

---

## Corpus & Tooling

### [GLOSS-FACTLATTICE] FactLattice / .lts

- term: FactLattice (`.lts`)
- definition: the queryable spec/decision format the corpus is authored in (successor to SMD) — nodes with typed edges, frontmatter, doctype tags, confidence, and the `change`/`context_for_change` primitive. Humans do NOT hand-edit `.lts`; an Intelligence composes them and humans read the rendered output. The parser/linter is a ComposeBus Service.
- lives-in: `families/services` (`svc`); the base grammar in `~/factlattice/`
- see-also: [GLOSS-MAGMA]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

### [GLOSS-MAGMA] MAGMA

- term: MAGMA (multi-corpus graph engine)
- definition: the engine that reads the FactLattice corpus as a MULTI-corpus partition — one `graph_index` per corpus, filtered by the domain suffix that already encodes the corpus. IDs are unique WITHIN a corpus, never globally; cross-corpus edges become a thin routing layer, not a rebuilt core. `store.py` supports a list of roots with a `corpus_id`.
- lives-in: `families/services` (`svc`); the engine at `~/factlattice/`
- see-also: [GLOSS-FACTLATTICE]
- relates-to: [SYSTEM:PLT-CONVENTIONS]
- part-of: [SYSTEM:PLT-GLOSSARY]

